msgstr "Ursache der Warnung"

#. Connection inspector: heading of the exits section.
msgctxt "adv_exits"
msgid "Exits"
msgstr "Exits"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the first choice of the verdict filter above the list of connections (routing decisions). Shows every connection, whatever its verdict. Short: it shares one row with Blocked, Tunnelled and Bypassed.
msgctxt "adv_filter_all"
msgid "All"
msgstr "Alle"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the verdict filter choice that shows only the connections that bypassed the tunnel (allowed, but sent directly from this device outside the VPN, for example by a split rule, so not protected). Short: it shares one row with All, Blocked and Tunnelled.
msgctxt "adv_filter_bypassed"
msgid "Bypassed"
msgstr "Am Tunnel vorbei"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the verdict filter choice that shows only the connections sent through the URnetwork tunnel (allowed and protected). Short: it shares one row with All, Blocked and Bypassed.
msgctxt "adv_filter_tunnelled"
msgid "Tunnelled"
msgstr "Getunnelt"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: label of the switch beside the search field that folds the list of connections into one row per host (with the count, the summed traffic and the latest decision). Clicking a host's row turns the switch off and searches for that host.
msgctxt "adv_group_by_host"
msgid "Group by host"
msgstr "Nach Host gruppieren"

#. Connection inspector: label of the host row.
msgctxt "adv_host"
msgid "Host"
msgstr "Host"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule allowing the connection's host from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_allowed"
msgid "This host will be allowed"
msgstr "Dieser Host wird zugelassen"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule blocking the connection's host from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_blocked"
msgid "This host will be blocked"
msgstr "Dieser Host wird blockiert"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a split rule sending the connection's host outside the VPN tunnel from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_bypassed"
msgid "This host will bypass the tunnel"
msgstr "Dieser Host wird am Tunnel vorbei geleitet"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule keeping the connection's host inside the VPN tunnel from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_tunnelled"
msgid "This host will use the tunnel"
msgstr "Dieser Host nutzt den Tunnel"

#. Connection inspector: heading of the inspector pane.
msgctxt "adv_inspector"
msgid "Inspector"
msgstr "Inspektor"

#. Kill switch: status while the change is being applied.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_applying"
msgid "Applying…"
msgstr "Wird angewendet…"

#. Kill switch: how to restore normal access while the block is armed.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_armed_way_out"
msgid "Turn the kill switch off to restore normal access without connecting."
msgstr "Schalte den Kill switch aus, um den normalen Zugriff ohne Verbindung wiederherzustellen."

#. Settings, kill switch: Disconnect always restores the internet; the switch only covers drops the user did not ask for.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_deliberate"
msgid "Pressing Disconnect always restores your internet straight away. The kill switch only applies to drops you did not ask for - a tunnel that stops carrying traffic, a network change, or the URnetwork service stopping."
msgstr "Trennen stellt das Internet immer sofort wieder her. Der Kill switch greift nur bei Abbrüchen, die du nicht angefordert hast - ein Tunnel, der keinen Verkehr mehr trägt, ein Netzwerkwechsel oder das Anhalten des URnetwork-Dienstes."

#. Settings, kill switch: what may leave the device while the switch is on, and the name-lookup window during a connection attempt.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_dns_window"
msgid "While it is on and nothing is connecting, nothing leaves this device - name lookups included. During a connection attempt, name lookups from any app on this device can leave in the clear so URnetwork can reach its servers; everything else stays blocked."
msgstr "Solange er an ist und nichts verbindet, verlässt nichts dieses Gerät - auch keine Namensauflösungen. Während eines Verbindungsversuchs dürfen Namensauflösungen jeder App auf diesem Gerät unverschlüsselt hinaus, damit URnetwork seine Server erreicht; alles andere bleibt blockiert."

#. Settings: explanation under the kill switch switch.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_note"
msgid "If the tunnel drops unexpectedly, block this device's traffic instead of letting it out unprotected."
msgstr "Wenn der Tunnel unerwartet abbricht, den Datenverkehr dieses Geräts blockieren, statt ihn ungeschützt hinauszulassen."

#. Kill switch: how to remove a block that is still in place when the device cannot reach the network; {command} is the shell command.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_recovery"
msgid "If this device cannot reach the network, a block installed earlier may still be in place; remove it with: {}"
msgstr "Wenn dieses Gerät das Netzwerk nicht erreicht, ist womöglich noch eine früher installierte Sperre aktiv; entferne sie mit: {}"

#. Kill switch status: in force and armed, only local traffic leaves until connected.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_armed"
msgid "In force: nothing but local network traffic leaves this device until you connect."
msgstr "In Kraft: Bis du dich verbindest, verlässt nur lokaler Netzwerkverkehr dieses Gerät."

#. Kill switch status: in force while connected, traffic is blocked if the tunnel drops.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_connected"
msgid "In force: if the tunnel drops, this device's traffic is blocked instead of going out unprotected."
msgstr "In Kraft: Bricht der Tunnel ab, wird der Datenverkehr dieses Geräts blockiert, statt ungeschützt hinauszugehen."

#. Kill switch status: the system service could not install the block.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_failed"
msgid "The URnetwork system service could not install the kill switch, so your traffic is NOT being blocked."
msgstr "Der URnetwork-Systemdienst konnte den Kill switch nicht installieren, der Datenverkehr wird also nicht blockiert."

#. Kill switch status: not in force, traffic is not blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_not_in_force"
msgid "The kill switch is NOT in force: your traffic is not being blocked."
msgstr "Der Kill switch ist NICHT in Kraft: Dein Datenverkehr wird nicht blockiert."

#. Kill switch status: nothing is blocked yet, takes effect on connect.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_pending"
msgid "Nothing is blocked yet — this takes effect the moment you connect."
msgstr "Noch ist nichts blockiert — das gilt ab dem Moment, in dem du dich verbindest."

#. Kill switch status: the switch is off but the service still has a block installed, so traffic is blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_still_installed"
msgid "The kill switch is off, but the URnetwork system service still has a block installed, so this device's traffic is being blocked."
msgstr "Der Kill switch ist aus, aber der URnetwork-Systemdienst hat noch eine Sperre installiert, sodass der Datenverkehr dieses Geräts blockiert wird."

#. Kill switch status: cannot be checked right now.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_unknown"
msgid "Whether the kill switch is in force cannot be checked right now."
msgstr "Ob der Kill switch in Kraft ist, lässt sich gerade nicht prüfen."

#. Kill switch: how to clear a block the service still has installed; {command} is the shell command to use if toggling does not work.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_still_installed_fix"
msgid "Turning the kill switch on and then off again asks the service to clear it; if that does not work, remove it with: {}"
msgstr "Den Kill switch ein- und wieder auszuschalten weist den Dienst an, sie zu entfernen; falls das nicht klappt, entferne sie mit: {}"

#. Connection inspector: label of the last routing decision row.
